\section{Introduction}
Deeplearning has revolutionized adversarial robustness research, as evidenced by body of work from goodfellow2014explaining to madry2018 Towards robust artificial intelligence. These studies utilize perturbed inputs to probe model weaknesses and generate counterexamples to improve weak areas. However, effectively targeting all weaknesses through a diverse array of counterexamples remains difficult. This paper investigates using diverse, rule-based noise as counterexamples to enhance model trustworthiness.

