The objective of this study is to evaluate whether Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) can accurately modify existing digital radiographs (DRX)s to simulate one or multiple pathologies simultaneously. Currently, there is a lack of public datasets offering DRXs with multiple superimposed conditions, a limitation that hinders research into diagnostic systems for such images and results in insufficient generalization when applying models trained on single-condition images to multi-condition cases. To address this, we proposed Generative Condition Addition (GCA), which utilizes a GAN to realistically alter DRXs by adding one or multiple conditions. GCA outperformed three state-of-the-art methods across all metrics. Furthermore, the model achieved an acceptable score on human perception studies, with an average of 73% of participants correctly identifying the injected condition, and 96% agreeing that the modified images were natural. The code for this project is available on GitHub.

